[Music]  Donald Trump was expected to testify  under oath Wednesday as part of the New  York attorney general's civil probe into  the Trump family business good morning  the attorney general has said that she  has uncovered significant evidence that  the Trump organization used fraudulent  property values in representations that  made two Banks insurers and tax entities  and they have uncovered evidence that  the trumps were directly involved in  this New York attorney general Leticia  James sent subpoenas to Trump and two of  his adult children Ivanka Trump and  Donald Trump Jr in December ordering  them to testify in closed-door  depositions the trumps have denied  wrongdoing the interview comes on the  heels of federal agents searching his  Florida residence Monday for a separate  investigation by the justice department  Corrine Ramey covers white-collar crime  for the Wall Street Journal and explains  what you need to know about the New York  attorney general's civil investigation  [Music]  the Attorney General's office has said  its probe began in March 2019 after  former Trump lawyer Michael Cohen  testified before Congress it was my  experience that Mr Trump inflated his  total assets when it served his purposes  such as trying to be listed amongst the  wealthiest people in Forbes and deflated  his assets  to reduce his real estate taxes Attorney  General James's office has since said  that Donald Trump made inaccurate  statements in financial documents for  multiple Properties by inflating his  assets this could lead to more favorable  terms from lenders or insurers it could  lead to bigger loans in 2015 and 2016  Trump's financial statements valued his  Triplex apartment in Trump Tower at 327  million dollars based on the assertion  that the triplex was 30 000 square feet  in size the Attorney General says the  actual size of the apartment was 10 996  square feet and that Trump even signed  documents confirming this in 2012.  according to the attorney general Alan  weisselberg the Chief Financial Officer  also admitted the value of the apartment  was overstated by 200 million the  Attorney General also says Trump falsely  valued Seven Springs a 213 acre property  in Westchester County New York that the  former president bought for 7.5 million  dollars in 1995 5. the Trump  organization had considered developing  the property but later scrapped the  plans Trump instead placed 158 Acres of  the land in a conservation easement  conservation easements are donating the  Land Development rights for a property  in exchange for tax benefits the  conservation easement portion of the  land was appraised at 21.1 million  dollars in 2016. and a lawyer for the  Attorney General's office said Seven  Springs LLC which is part of the Trump  organization claimed a 21.1 million  dollar tax deduction for the easement in  tax year 2015. it was higher than  previous valuations this allowed him to  get a larger tax benefit according to  the attorney general a spokeswoman for  the Trump organization said attorney  general James's allegations were  baseless and the trumps have claimed  that the subpoenas could be used to  improperly gather evidence for a  separate criminal investigation by the  Manhattan district attorney which has  led to indictments charging the Trump  organization and its Finance  Alan weiselberg with tax crimes that  investigation is continuing and it has  looked at similar issues in terms of  deflating and inflating assets lawyers  for the trumps also argued that the  office of Attorney General James a  Democrat had unfairly targeted the  former president and his children for  political reasons they point to  statement she made during her campaign  when she has said she'll investigate the  trumps and sort of made this a campaign  priority the trumps had attempted to  avoid testifying by asking courts to  quash the subpoenas but the courts ruled  in favor of the Attorney General and  said that the subpoenas were valid so  the trumps ran out of legal options and  now they need to testify Warriors for  the New York attorney general have  indicated that they could file a civil  lawsuit but it's unclear who the  defendants would be it could be the  Trump organization it could be Trump  himself or other company Executives or  employees it could be his kids typically  these lawsuits they take several years  to go through the courts and they it  could end in a settlement or a trial and  typically the penalties are Financial  foreign  [Music]

